A||||8||Jncomutt||Steering wheel wobble, Car Pulls WAY right||||1||
Z||000000||Jncomutt||10-15-2001||11:16 AM||||I had previously noticed a little wobble and shake in my steering wheel on the highway and didn't think much of it.  Perhaps it was just worn bushings or something else that comes with the car being old, or no power assist, I didn't really know.<P>Now, it seems all of a sudden, my steering wheel shakes Very hard.  To the point where I have to take my watch off because the links rattle so much it drives me crazy.  My car also pulls right now.  I have to drive with it a turned to the left to keep it going straight.  But when I let go, The top of the steering wheel turns itself to what would be about 2 o clock.  When I go to keep the car straight, its not just holding the wheel at the right place, you actually have to use a bit of energy to keep it there, and it constantly trys tugging the wheel right.<P>Any ideas??  Just a misalignment??  Bent A-arms or something?  One of the right side calipers??<P>I have heated spring on the front of my car.  Been like that for about 8 months now.  No other front end problems before this, just thought I'd add the info incase it helps.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fie Ro||10-15-2001||11:30 AM||||When the car pulls to the right it is a misalignment. When your steeringwheel vibrates it is a bad balanced wheel. So I guess you hit a curb or something but I should check your suspension. I once hit a curb and blew a tire. no suspension damage. Check the outer steeringrod for movement.<P>------------------<BR>-The Beauty & The Beast-<BR>1987 Pontiac Fiero GT & <BR>1977 Dodge W200||||reg||1
Z||000002||Master_Sushi||10-15-2001||11:43 AM||||You didn't curb the car or anything? Sounds like your alignment is way off. A really bad alignment will even cause the stearing wheel to shake. If its this bad I would think it would be noticeable just by looking at all the wheels and seeing if they point in the right direction.<P>If you alignment isnt the problum it could be bearings or something. Im my old 88 the front right bearing was so bad the car pulled to the right and kind of wobbled.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jncomutt||10-15-2001||11:59 AM||||I haven't hit a curb.  What I do know is that I take left turns around this corner that has a little dip in it.  When I go over it fast, the car gets really light, then comes down hard just as it bites the road and rips thru the turn.  Could this 'abuse' sort of thing have done it???<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Master_Sushi||10-15-2001||12:08 PM||||I dont think taking corners fast would hurt a fiero. Thats what fiero do best!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>If your geting airborne or something when taking this turn... Ya then that might not be good.<BR>If I were you, I'd just take the car to a shop and get a 4 wheel alignment. They dont cost that much, and its most likely the problum. Even if that dosent fix it, it probably needs one anyway.<P>Maybe jack the car up and check each wheel for play. If you have any thats also a problum. Also check all your bushings while you have the car up. They might be worn out.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jncomutt||10-16-2001||08:44 PM||||Ok... Just got back from the shop.. Got a 4 wheel alignment, 4 tires balanced and remounted, and a full suspension check.  They said everything looked fine.  I got in, drive it home, it still pulls hard right.  Taking the rear brakes apart tomorrow, see if they're any drag and try the Archie Adjust shim thingy.  Hopefully that will solve it.. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||10-17-2001||10:37 AM||||lots of other things can do it too. try swapping the left and right tires (dont laugh), may have a brake caliper dragging, bad rack. Could even have a piece of stone or something jammed in brake shoes.Bad Wheel bearing.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 10-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||the need for speed||10-17-2001||06:25 PM||||mine does the same thing ever since I got it. I am thinking it could be a worn out rack and pinon||||reg||1
Z||000008||Scott||10-18-2001||12:36 AM||||Could also be a bad inner tie rod. ||||reg||1
